[32m+[m[32m# EduNexus AI — Python Track[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA full-stack, Python-only adaptive learning platform: a real knowledge-graph[m
[32m+[m[32mcurriculum, a quiz engine that updates mastery scores, an AI career-match[m
[32m+[m[32mengine, an auto-generated roadmap, and a REPL-style tutor that adapts its[m
[32m+[m[32mexplanation depth to what you actually know.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis is the **core loop, built end to end** — not a mockup. Every button[m
[32m+[m[32mcalls a real API backed by a real database.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mbackend/   FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + JWT auth (SQLite by default, Postgres-ready)[m
[32m+[m[32mfrontend/  React + Vite, talks to the backend over a REST API[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What's real vs. what's a deliberate simplification[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Real**: JWT auth, password hashing, a relational schema, server-side[m
[32m+[m[32m  scoring/recommendation/roadmap logic, persistent per-user knowledge state,[m
[32m+[m[32m  CORS, environment-based config.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Mock "AI"**: there's no LLM call and no trained ML model. The "AI" is[m
[32m+[m[32m  deterministic logic — weighted scoring, a prerequisite-graph traversal,[m
[32m+[m[32m  rule-based recommendations with explicit explanations. This is intentional:[m
[32m+[m[32m  it's honest, fully explainable, and demoable with zero API keys. Swapping[m
[32m+[m[32m  in a real model later (e.g. for the tutor) means replacing `tutor_respond()`[m
[32m+[m[32m  in `backend/app/engine.py` with an LLM call — the rest of the architecture[m
[32m+[m[32m  doesn't need to change.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Trust model for quizzes**: to keep instant feedback (see the correct[m
[32m+[m[32m  answer and explanation the moment you pick one, like most learning apps),[m
[32m+[m[32m  the quiz-generation endpoint sends the correct answer to the client, and[m
[32m+[m[32m  the client reports back which questions it got right. A production[m
[32m+[m[32m  version handling graded/high-stakes assessments would grade purely[m
[32m+[m[32m  server-side and never send the answer key to the browser.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Quick start[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 1. Backend (FastAPI)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mcd backend[m
[32m+[m[32mpython3 -m venv .venv[m
[32m+[m[32msource .venv/bin/activate        # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate[m
[32m+[m[32mpip install -r requirements.txt[m
[32m+[m[32mcp .env.example .env             # edit JWT_SECRET before any real deployment[m
[32m+[m[32muvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOr just run `./run.sh` (creates the venv, installs, and starts it).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe API is now at `http://localhost:8000` — interactive docs at[m
[32m+[m[32m`http://localhost:8000/docs`. On first boot it creates `edunexus.db`[m
[32m+[m[32m(SQLite) and seeds a demo student automatically.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2. Frontend (React + Vite)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mcd frontend[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm install[m
[32m+[m[32mcp .env.example .env             # only needed if the backend isn't on :8000[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run dev[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen `http://localhost:5173`. Click **"Try instant demo"** to log in as a[m
[32m+[m[32mpre-populated demo student with realistic mastery data, or register a real[m
[32m+[m[32maccount and start from a blank knowledge state.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Switching to Postgres[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEdit `backend/.env`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/edunexus[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThen uncomment `psycopg2-binary` in `requirements.txt` and reinstall. No[m
[32m+[m[32mcode changes needed — SQLAlchemy handles both dialects identically here.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What's implemented (core loop, done properly)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Auth**: register / login / instant demo login, JWT bearer tokens,[m
[32m+[m[32m  bcrypt password hashing.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Knowledge graph**: 20 Python concepts (syntax → data types → control[m
[32m+[m[32m  flow → functions → OOP → decorators/algorithms) as a real prerequisite[m
[32m+[m[32m  DAG, rendered as an interactive node graph.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Quiz engine**: 40-question bank across all 20 concepts, filterable by[m
[32m+[m[32m  topic/difficulty/count, server-recorded attempts, live mastery updates.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Career AI**: 5 Python-track roles with weighted skill requirements,[m
[32m+[m[32m  computed match %, and skill-gap breakdowns.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Roadmap**: auto-generated month-by-month plan from the real[m
[32m+[m[32m  prerequisite closure of whichever career goal you set.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Nexus Tutor**: keyword-matches your question to a concept and replies[m
[32m+[m[32m  at beginner/intermediate/advanced depth based on your mastery of that[m
[32m+[m[32m  specific topic — with chat history persisted per user.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Dashboard**: streak, knowledge score, placement readiness, top career[m
[32m+[m[32m  match, today's plan, knowledge-decay alerts, and explainable[m
[32m+[m[32m  recommendations ("why am I seeing this?" shows the actual factors used).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What's intentionally out of scope for this build[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPer the agreed scope, this ships the **core loop only** — dashboard,[m
[32m+[m[32mknowledge graph, AI tutor, quiz, career match, roadmap. The wider original[m
[32m+[m[32mspec (marketplace, mentorship, faculty/admin dashboards, resume analyzer,[m
[32m+[m[32minterview simulator, company-prep modules, etc.) is not built here. The[m
[32m+[m[32marchitecture (routers, engine module, curriculum data) is structured so[m
[32m+[m[32mthose could be added as new routers + frontend pages without restructuring[m
[32m+[m[32mwhat exists.[m
[32m+[m
